WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.690
- It's my pleasure today to introduce

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.010
Professor Vicente L. Rafael,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.560
who as you know is about as well-respected

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.270
and well-known as it is
possible to be in academia.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.020
And we are really delighted
to be able to host him

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.650
in our modest Brown Bag
Series here at Yale.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.460
Many of you will know his
justifiably famous works

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.230
on the historical and cultural politics

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.280
of the colonial and
post-colonial Philippines

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.037
including modern classics such
as "Contracting Colonialism,"

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.137
"White Love and Other
Events in Filipino History"

00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:43.580
"The Promise of the Foreign,"
and "Motherless Tongues."

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.190
He's also the editor of
several important collections

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.110
in Southeast Asian studies.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.470
And if you go visit the Duke
University press website

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.940
and search Vicente L. Rafael

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.030
you'll pretty much see
that he is the central core

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.760
of their post-colonial studies series,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.330
really in some way it's
brings Duke's reputation

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.150
in that field into fruition.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.260
Now, me personally,

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.520
I first learned of professor
Raphael's importance

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.030
when I was a PhD student at Cornell,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.140
when I had the privilege of taking courses

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.300
with Benedict Anderson
and James T. Siegel.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.010
And although Ben and Jim are
rarely impressed by anyone

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.070
they would always speak in reverend tones

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.010
when they would recount the stories

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.260
of their greatest student Vicente Raphael.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.350
Perhaps I would say the
only of their students

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.780
who could encounter their charisma

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.070
without being shocked into submission.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.270
The rest of us, when we
would meet Jim and Ben

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.463
would become sort of silent to use,

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.740
the way Jim might phrase it,

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.700
we'd become like corpses in
the face of their charisma.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.420
But Vince, it seems has been
able to harness the energy

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.550
of their teaching without
becoming devoured by it.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.410
Today's talk offers a sneak
preview of a forthcoming book

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.230
on the politics and aesthetics
of the Duterte regime.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.727
It's entitled, "The Sovereign Trickster:

00:02:09.727 --> 00:02:12.700
"Death And Laughter in
the Age of Duterte."

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.600
And that book will soon be published

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.750
by Duke University press.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.780
Please join me today in
welcoming Vicente Raphael

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.089
for his talk entitled "Duterte's Phallus:

00:02:23.089 --> 00:02:28.089
"On the Aesthetics of
Authoritarian Vulgarity."

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.840
And I will share the screen

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.743
and once this sheet screen is
shared he will begin his talk.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.210
- It's really a pleasure to be here

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.390
even if it's just a
virtual kind of meeting.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:42.100
I noticed many, many friends

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.010
and colleagues that I
haven't seen in a while.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.833
So hello everyone.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.110
Thanks so much for coming.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.460
And again, thank you for
facilitating this Erik and Chris

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.430
and the rest of the students and staff

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.000
at the Southeast Asia program.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.300
As Erik mentioned this
is a talk that spun out

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.530
of one of the chapters
of my forthcoming book.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.370
And if you would like during the Q and A

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.180
to sort of expand some
of the arguments I make

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.210
in this chapter and connected
with everything else

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.480
I've been trying to figure out in the book

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.733
I'd be more than happy to.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.713
So let me begin by,

00:03:31.902 --> 00:03:33.603
first of all by locating my paper.

00:03:42.036 --> 00:03:44.369
Okay, one of the things that

00:03:49.176 --> 00:03:52.450
if you've sort of even
briefly been following

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.857
events in the Philippines,
since the election of Duterte

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.803
two things you notice

00:03:57.803 --> 00:04:01.330
one is that he remains enormously popular

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.480
despite all the sort
of arguably disastrous

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:10.200
and near genocidal policies
he's adopted in the Philippines.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.350
And the second thing is that

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.300
he's also sort of remarkably vulgar

00:04:15.492 --> 00:04:18.970
and people have tried to sort
of establish the connection

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:22.373
between his popularity and
his vulgarity, his obscenity.

00:04:23.408 --> 00:04:28.383
And in this paper I sort of
try to connect the two as well.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.410
In terms of asking a very basic question

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.040
which is what are the sources
of his symbolic authority?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.070
How has he managed to
occupy such a central place

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.620
in the imaginative life of Filipinos,

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.920
both supporters and critics alike,

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.363
as well as those at home and abroad?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.260
And one of the ways in which

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.800
the president lays claim to both national

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.890
and global attention is
through his stories and jokes.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.560
I mean, he's a consummate storyteller.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.380
And so the humor comes
as part of the stories

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.040
that he likes to tell.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.470
He's widely known for his
irreverence and body humor

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.970
that constitute important
elements of his governing style.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.660
And it's really that
I def want connect.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.630
I want the connection between
his storytelling abilities

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.460
and his governing style.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.865
His stories reveal a reliance on invective

00:05:23.865 --> 00:05:26.320
and an obsession with obscenity.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.390
He also makes frequent
references to genitalia,

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.940
his as well as those of his critics,

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.540
to the delight of his listeners.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.170
He revels in what the
philosopher, a Shield of Bombay

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.500
calls an aesthetic of vulgarity

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.090
that has the effect of establishing

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.390
a relationship of conviviality

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.470
between himself and his audience,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.880
which results is a kind
of intimate tyranny,

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.810
much of it's centered on
the tales of his phallus

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.020
as it encounters the world.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.120
So, for example,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.883
and here we could start
with the next slide.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.838
For example, in his campaign
events in April, 2016

00:06:03.838 --> 00:06:06.900
Duterte addressed the Makati Business Club

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.130
which is about a sedate
and as conservative setting

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.460
as you can imagine,

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.000
made up of wealthy
businessmen in the country,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.240
rather than talk about
his economic policies,

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.150
though he regaled the
audience with stories

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.560
about his use of Viagra.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.563
So he says, for example,

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:30.048
well I'm separated from my
wife, annulled, so I'm useless.

00:06:30.048 --> 00:06:33.680
So I'm not useless, I'm not paralyzed.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.570
What am I supposed to do with
my goddam thing down there?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.010
Let it hang forever?

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.000
Well, there's no drama going on,

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.490
I drank Viagra and then it stood up.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:46.070
Oh let's not kid ourselves,
I am giving it to you raw.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.163
I thought you were all the same age here.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.440
So he starts with a story, right?

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:56.420
And here you can see what
Duterte shares with men

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.080
of a certain age and
considerable influence,

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.500
his story about his experience

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.970
of emasculation followed by rejuvenation.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:08.100
Thanks to appeal, he regains his heart on

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.650
the material evidence of a phallic power

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.170
that he thought he had lost.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:15.460
Laughter ensues as he
discursively shows to the men

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.800
a part of himself that
should have been hidden.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:22.200
His obscenity consists of
making the private public

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.080
reaching below to
connect with those above.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.610
It is this sexual politics
from below that binds Duterte

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:32.650
to these men, along with
a sprinkling of women

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.300
who joined in the laughter.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.690
Together they share a common fantasy

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.330
about the authoritarian phallus

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:41.680
as something they can
imaginatively access,

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.350
and the prospective pleasures
of a drug induced erection

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.730
beginning with that of Duterte's.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.630
But as we shall see,
in other examples below

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.910
the presidential phallus comes across

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.480
not only as an instrument of pleasure,

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.510
but also as a sign of terror.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:02.760
In another campaign stop
at a large sports complex

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.382
in Caisson City around the
same time around early 2016

00:08:05.382 --> 00:08:10.382
Duterte tells a story that
reverberated around the world,

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.270
and some of you may have
remembered this particular tale.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:19.340
He says that while he was
a mayor in Davao in 1989

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.910
there occurred a bloody
prison siege in Davao City.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.940
Among the dead was one of the hostages

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.430
taken by the prisoners,

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:30.680
a 36 year old Australia
missionary, Jacqueline Hamill.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.030
According to Duterte,

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.860
she was repeatedly raped by the prisoners

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:37.290
along with other women
hostages before being killed.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:42.290
But rather than evoke Patheos,
the sight of Hamill’s corpse

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.890
stares desire in the mayor.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.990
And if it can have the next slide, please.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.610
All the women were raped
during that first assault

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.930
because they retreated the
bodies they used as shields.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.240
One of them was a corpse

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:01.322
of the Australian woman lay minister.

00:09:01.322 --> 00:09:03.350
Tsk, this was a problem.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.940
When the bodies were brought
out, they were wrapped.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.450
I looked at her face, son of a bitch,

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.830
she looked like a
beautiful American actress.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.640
Son of a bitch , what a waste!

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.940
And son of a bitch here is

00:09:14.777 --> 00:09:17.070
it was a very common Filipino curse.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.240
What came to mind was they
raped her, they took turns.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.030
I was angry because she was
raped, that's one thing,

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.680
but she was so beautiful,

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.480
the mayor should have
gone first son of a bitch,

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.090
what a waste, Sayang.

00:09:30.795 --> 00:09:35.180
Okay, so much for that slide.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:39.477
Here Hamill's rape and
death is used by Duterte

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:44.660
as a setup for a joke about
himself, more specifically

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:48.470
about the arousal and
frustration of his lost.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.160
He sees her dead body
and her beautiful face

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.520
and he feels like he should
have been the first in line

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.620
to assault her.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:59.020
Instead, he comes too late
and isn't able to come at all.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:02.510
It is his failure to assert
his claim on the woman's body

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.010
that is presumably taken by his audience

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.950
as the object of hilarity.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.910
Seeing her dead body fills him
neither would rage nor grief

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.680
but with a desire that
cannot be fulfilled.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.720
He is unable to discharge
his authority as it were.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.250
The horror of the scene is just displaced

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.060
into a story about a mayor

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.940
lamenting the failure of his phallic power

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.030
rather than the erectile victory

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:28.910
celebrated in the first story,

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:32.840
the second ends with a
punchline Sayang, what a pity

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:37.720
receded by the cuss word
Hutangnya, son of a bitch.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.020
But all is not lost.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:42.560
Duterte's disclosure of desire unfulfilled

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.560
and phallic authority
undercut produces a payback.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.800
The audience laughs and their
laughter compensates him

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:52.253
for his lost power.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.323
It returns to him, both the
pleasure and the authority

00:11:00.611 --> 00:11:02.410
that the dead prisoners
and the woman's corpse

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.490
had deprived him, unable to pull rank.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.510
The mayor is nevertheless rewarded

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:11.110
with the people's recognition
of his narrative performance.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.850
Reports to the story drew sharp rebukes

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.770
from feminists human rights advocates

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.760
and the Australian and U.S Embassy

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.920
as well as many other quarters.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:25.660
But among most of the electorate
his popularity soared.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.510
Horrifying his critics but
delighting his supporters

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.814
with his pungent shamelessness,

00:11:30.814 --> 00:11:34.720
Duterte's bad language and
obscene stories were crucial

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.283
to propelling him to the presidency.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:39.900
And tracking his jokes,

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:42.970
we can see a set of obsessions
built around the question,

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.883
who gets to own the phallus,

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.050
who gets to wield it and for what purpose?

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.570
Here the phallus should be understood

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:55.050
less as a biological things
synonymous with a penis

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:59.070
as a symbolic weapon for
asserting autocratic authority

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:03.960
and patriarchal prerogatives
over women and men alike.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.370
Like guns, cars are wealth,

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.460
the phallus can be used
to impress and to threaten

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.580
to unify and to disperse,

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:16.100
to induce pleasure but
also to coerce submission.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.410
Duterte routinely threatens
to castrate his opponents,

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:22.930
even as he repeatedly reveals
his generous endowment.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:27.520
He used to event imagine hearts
and shore up fragile ego,

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.610
Duterte phallus proved effective

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.920
in shutting down his opposition.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:33.780
The presidential phallus, however,

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:36.960
is far from being an unassailable force.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.990
As we saw in the rape story above,

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.380
it can also be blunted by other men

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:43.890
and women whose death frustrated

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.520
Duterte's assertion of his privileges.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:50.550
Indeed, Duterte is notorious
for joking about rape

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.700
as a way of reasserting his ability

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.890
to police women's behavior

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.120
and enlist men into affirming

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:01.430
the sexism that buttresses
his authoritarian imagination.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:05.390
Hence, when critics point out
that contrary to his claims

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:09.400
crime and Davao while he was
a mayor had actually gone up

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.810
especially rape.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.720
He retorts that wherever
there are beautiful women

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.540
there will be plenty of rape.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.690
Along the same lines he
also spoke approvingly

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:22.040
of men who had the
balls to rape candidates

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:26.020
for miss universe in exchange
for facing certain punishment.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.570
Women are raped, not simply
because they are women

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.120
for Duterte, it is because
they are "beautiful."

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.400
It is as if their beauty is a challenge

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.130
that has to be faced down,

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.800
a provocation its proper place

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:42.513
under the rule in the
service of the phallus.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.508
The philosopher, Kate Mann

00:13:45.508 --> 00:13:49.700
has a very interesting and
useful description of misogyny.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.090
And perhaps let me just cite it here

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:56.540
as a way of framing the Duterte's
own particular misogyny.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:00.457
He says, "Misogyny is what
happens when women break ranks

00:14:00.457 --> 00:14:03.897
"or rules and disrupt
the patriarchal order.

00:14:03.897 --> 00:14:06.697
"They tend to be perceived
as uppity unruly,

00:14:06.697 --> 00:14:08.667
"out of line or insubordinate.

00:14:08.667 --> 00:14:11.047
"Misogyny isn't simply hateful,

00:14:11.047 --> 00:14:14.687
"it produces social costs
on noncompliant women.

00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:18.957
"Think of misogyny then as
the law enforcement branch

00:14:18.957 --> 00:14:21.137
