01:09:57.380 --> 01:09:58.723
- Yeah, tuklong.

01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:04.710
- We originally had a
question form Rhodah Galamba

01:10:04.710 --> 01:10:09.429
but he sent me a note saying
his question was already asked

01:10:09.429 --> 01:10:11.779
and answered so we'll go
straight to Jim Scott.

01:10:14.340 --> 01:10:15.440
- Hi, Jim, Jim.

01:10:20.330 --> 01:10:22.253
- Jim you just need to unmute briefly.

01:10:24.250 --> 01:10:25.440
- Can you hear me now?

01:10:25.440 --> 01:10:27.378
- [Vincente] Yeah, yeah, hi Jim.

01:10:27.378 --> 01:10:31.120
- Hi Vince, I can't wait for the book.

01:10:31.120 --> 01:10:35.480
So it's exciting to get a glimpse into it.

01:10:35.480 --> 01:10:38.550
I had a re a rather simple question

01:10:38.550 --> 01:10:43.550
and that is the use of the word joke.

01:10:46.460 --> 01:10:49.593
Your stories don't sound like jokes.

01:10:50.600 --> 01:10:52.640
And there it's a raconteur,

01:10:52.640 --> 01:10:54.140
it's just sort of personal history

01:10:54.140 --> 01:10:57.820
with all of the edges that you point out,

01:10:57.820 --> 01:11:02.710
but it's not the at least the kind of,

01:11:02.710 --> 01:11:07.360
maybe I'm looking at it
through two western eyes

01:11:07.360 --> 01:11:12.360
of a joke with a punchline and
a sort of suspense and so on.

01:11:13.570 --> 01:11:18.170
And so it strikes me that
what Duterte is doing

01:11:19.060 --> 01:11:22.480
is maybe something other than a joke

01:11:22.480 --> 01:11:27.480
that we need a kind of special category.

01:11:28.080 --> 01:11:30.840
And that therefore it's a little odd

01:11:30.840 --> 01:11:35.513
to sort of put it in the
Freudian joke, category, right?

01:11:36.930 --> 01:11:40.970
Anyway, what are the other ways

01:11:40.970 --> 01:11:45.970
in which one might think
of what Duterte is doing

01:11:46.200 --> 01:11:51.200
and it also occurred to me to wonder in,

01:11:52.960 --> 01:11:55.083
for ordinary Filipinos,

01:11:57.280 --> 01:12:02.280
this kind of talk would it
be confined to men drinking?

01:12:05.910 --> 01:12:10.910
Would it, what kinds of social contexts

01:12:11.210 --> 01:12:16.210
would this kind of
storytelling be confined?

01:12:19.693 --> 01:12:23.580
We're not a kind of
presidential repertoire.

01:12:28.480 --> 01:12:29.680
- You're absolutely right.

01:12:29.680 --> 01:12:31.820
These are the kinds of stories men,

01:12:31.820 --> 01:12:35.120
and some women would tell around

01:12:35.120 --> 01:12:38.193
you know, drinking sessions, for example.

01:12:39.160 --> 01:12:41.323
And so it's not unusual.

01:12:42.640 --> 01:12:43.473
What happens though

01:12:43.473 --> 01:12:46.110
is that those drinking
sessions are usually circles,

01:12:46.110 --> 01:12:47.530
close circles.

01:12:47.530 --> 01:12:51.950
And it's very rare that
they come come across

01:12:51.950 --> 01:12:54.660
much more publicly in a
in a way you could argue

01:12:54.660 --> 01:12:59.660
that Duterte's storytelling
has sort of created this

01:13:00.760 --> 01:13:05.040
has nationalized drinking circle, right?

01:13:05.040 --> 01:13:08.210
Which used to be very local,
very small, very intimate.

01:13:08.210 --> 01:13:13.210
He's turned an intimate
gathering into very public

01:13:13.400 --> 01:13:15.800
sort of situation.

01:13:15.800 --> 01:13:18.490
The second point you make
is extremely interesting.

01:13:18.490 --> 01:13:23.310
Are these jokes properly
sort of thought of

01:13:23.310 --> 01:13:25.490
or is there something is another category

01:13:25.490 --> 01:13:27.120
that we can use for it?

01:13:27.120 --> 01:13:28.637
You know, I've struggled with that.

01:13:28.637 --> 01:13:31.270
And one of the things that I use

01:13:31.270 --> 01:13:33.440
as you can tell from the title of the book

01:13:33.440 --> 01:13:35.320
is tricksterism, right?

01:13:35.320 --> 01:13:40.320
I mean, I refer to Duterte
as a trickster figure,

01:13:40.799 --> 01:13:43.120
which probably would
be again would connect

01:13:43.120 --> 01:13:44.943
to more Southeast Asian context.

01:13:45.810 --> 01:13:48.455
And the thing about the
trickster figure as you know

01:13:48.455 --> 01:13:51.460
it's very widespread in the Philippines,

01:13:51.460 --> 01:13:53.330
it's very widespread, it's Southeast Asia.

01:13:53.330 --> 01:13:55.880
There isn't a single
Southeast Asian country

01:13:55.880 --> 01:13:59.540
that doesn't have some
figure of the trickster

01:13:59.540 --> 01:14:03.250
and the trickster it's a very
it's a very sort of uncanny

01:14:03.250 --> 01:14:05.450
or very canny figure, I should stay

01:14:05.450 --> 01:14:08.330
that combines aggressiveness

01:14:08.330 --> 01:14:10.920
with a certain kind of attractiveness

01:14:10.920 --> 01:14:14.400
that is funny but also cruel,

01:14:14.400 --> 01:14:18.560
that is predatory but also
in some ways subversive,

01:14:18.560 --> 01:14:21.160
in other words all these
different characteristics

01:14:21.160 --> 01:14:22.413
that we associate with Duterte

01:14:22.413 --> 01:14:25.000
that you can find in the trickster figure,

01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:27.070
which is very different, say
from the trickster figure

01:14:27.070 --> 01:14:28.920
that you might have a native American

01:14:30.070 --> 01:14:33.660
sort of contexts, but in the Philippines

01:14:33.660 --> 01:14:36.150
a trickster figure is omnipresent.

01:14:36.150 --> 01:14:38.930
And I think that that's
what you get with Duterte

01:14:38.930 --> 01:14:41.210
is not so much the concept.

01:14:41.210 --> 01:14:43.400
Well, he is a storyteller,
yes, that's true.

01:14:43.400 --> 01:14:46.690
But not so much a jokester
but more of a trickster.

01:14:46.690 --> 01:14:49.300
And my use of Freud is
really an attempt to,

01:14:49.300 --> 01:14:54.300
in some ways get at the
politics of this tricksterism

01:14:55.390 --> 01:14:57.570
of this jokester because
I do think that freight is

01:14:57.570 --> 01:14:59.960
so, I mean it's whatever criticism

01:14:59.960 --> 01:15:01.560
you might lodge against them.

01:15:01.560 --> 01:15:04.540
I still do think that he
was very very much keenly

01:15:04.540 --> 01:15:09.540
aware of the power of
not just storytelling,

01:15:09.760 --> 01:15:11.850
but of humor.

01:15:11.850 --> 01:15:13.201
And it's very interesting,

01:15:13.201 --> 01:15:15.390
'cause I hadn't read
jokes in the relationship

01:15:15.390 --> 01:15:18.310
to the unconscious for years, for decades.

01:15:18.310 --> 01:15:19.850
and when I read it, I was surprised.

01:15:19.850 --> 01:15:22.910
I think something like 80% of
the jokes are anti-semitic.

01:15:22.910 --> 01:15:26.350
I mean, all Jewish jokes,
you know, and he revels,

01:15:26.350 --> 01:15:30.013
in telling me his these Jewish jokes.

01:15:31.250 --> 01:15:34.580
And I mean, it really struck me as unusual

01:15:34.580 --> 01:15:37.190
to anybody that was a tricksterism.

01:15:37.190 --> 01:15:40.190
And then this idea of sort of elevating

01:15:40.190 --> 01:15:42.900
a certain intimate acts of convention

01:15:42.900 --> 01:15:46.343
defining exchanges to a national level.

01:15:50.237 --> 01:15:51.070
- Yeah, thank you.

01:15:51.070 --> 01:15:54.071
We're approaching our 1:20 mark.

01:15:54.071 --> 01:15:57.200
And so I think I'll gracefully
bring it to a close here.

01:15:57.200 --> 01:15:59.650
This has been a really
dynamic talk followed

01:15:59.650 --> 01:16:03.500
by a really dynamic Q and A period.

01:16:03.500 --> 01:16:05.010
So I just want to thank you for that.

01:16:05.010 --> 01:16:07.190
Before we say goodbye formerly

01:16:07.190 --> 01:16:09.050
you were mentioning drinking circles.

01:16:09.050 --> 01:16:12.930
So I thought I would
take a moment to announce

01:16:12.930 --> 01:16:17.930
the next Brown Bag in
two weeks on March 17th,

01:16:18.080 --> 01:16:20.630
which will be about the melancholic play

01:16:20.630 --> 01:16:22.310
of alcohol drinking Lee Su-min men

01:16:22.310 --> 01:16:24.640
on the China Myanmar border.

01:16:24.640 --> 01:16:27.440
So those of you who are
interested in this topic,

01:16:27.440 --> 01:16:31.150
please join us with
that said, oh go ahead.

01:16:31.150 --> 01:16:32.690
- Yeah, just one more thing about

01:16:32.690 --> 01:16:35.363
this whole question of
drinking and intimacy.

01:16:36.860 --> 01:16:39.100
One of the chapters in the book

01:16:39.100 --> 01:16:40.930
talks about the problem of intimacy

01:16:40.930 --> 01:16:42.280
and to making of community

01:16:43.365 --> 01:16:48.365
as it relates to Duterte's
anti-drug program.

01:16:49.890 --> 01:16:51.850
You know, as some of you might know

01:16:51.850 --> 01:16:54.960
one of the ways in Duterte's

01:16:54.960 --> 01:16:58.810
policy works is to what he
calls operation talk on.

01:16:58.810 --> 01:17:01.430
That is to say he has to police

01:17:01.430 --> 01:17:03.620
in conjunction with local officials,

01:17:03.620 --> 01:17:07.180
build a list of actual
and suspected drug users

01:17:07.180 --> 01:17:11.080
and drug dealers and this
essentially becomes the kill list.

01:17:11.080 --> 01:17:13.340
Now, the question is how
does he develop this list?

01:17:13.340 --> 01:17:14.200
Well he does so,

01:17:14.200 --> 01:17:17.230
because everybody knows
everybody else in the community.

01:17:17.230 --> 01:17:18.916
It's through intimacy

01:17:18.916 --> 01:17:21.790
that you have the
development of community.

01:17:21.790 --> 01:17:23.860
So the very conditions

01:17:23.860 --> 01:17:26.700
for creating community
become the very conditions

01:17:26.700 --> 01:17:29.740
for exposing it to this
sort of ongoing danger.

01:17:29.740 --> 01:17:31.133
And for this reason,

01:17:33.773 --> 01:17:34.750
rather than imagined community

01:17:34.750 --> 01:17:37.010
that Ben Anderson, you
know famously talked about

01:17:37.010 --> 01:17:38.280
what you get into Philippines

01:17:38.280 --> 01:17:41.770
is what I call an auto-immune community,

01:17:41.770 --> 01:17:43.720
a community of auto-immunity.

01:17:43.720 --> 01:17:47.910
You know where the community
in order to come into being

01:17:47.910 --> 01:17:50.040
actually enacts the very things

01:17:50.040 --> 01:17:52.830
that endangers it from within so

01:17:52.830 --> 01:17:55.240
and I think that's just a
tragedy, that is the tragedy

01:17:55.240 --> 01:17:58.610
and that is the horrific sort
of consequences of having

01:17:58.610 --> 01:18:03.550
someone like Duterte, you know
do this authoritarian drug.

01:18:03.550 --> 01:18:04.610
It's not the first time

01:18:04.610 --> 01:18:06.170
and it's not gonna be the last time,

01:18:06.170 --> 01:18:09.250
but with Duterte you have the
most dramatic manifestation

01:18:09.250 --> 01:18:10.973
of this audio Indian community.

01:18:11.970 --> 01:18:15.340
So that's maybe a way to end this.

01:18:15.340 --> 01:18:17.345
- That's a brilliant way to end it.

01:18:17.345 --> 01:18:19.230
So just join me, everyone

01:18:19.230 --> 01:18:22.420
and thanking professor Rafael
for this fantastic talk.

01:18:22.420 --> 01:18:24.030
I'll stop the recording now

01:18:24.030 --> 01:18:27.583
and then we can just linger
to say a polite goodbye.

